From: NanoKVM build <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] licheerv-nano: define ramdisk_addr_r and bound bootm relocation

The NanoKVM image boots via extlinux with a separate initramfs (INITRD
/initramfs), but mainline's licheerv_nano.h env defines only
kernel_addr_r/fdt_addr_r/scriptaddr. pxe_utils' label_boot() loads the
kernel, then fails get_relfile_envaddr("ramdisk_addr_r") and SKIPS the
whole label ("Skipping nanokvm for failure retrieving initrd"), leaving
the board stalled at the U-Boot prompt right after "Retrieving file:
/Image".

0x84000000 (64 MiB into the 256 MiB DRAM at 0x80000000) is clear of
scriptaddr (0x80c00000), the kernel at 0x81000000 (~11 MiB Image, and
booti relocates it down to 0x80200000), and the FDT at 0x82000000.

bootm_size caps where boot_ramdisk_high()/boot_relocate_fdt() may then
move them. ramdisk_addr_r is only the *load* address; with no bound U-Boot
relocates both to the top of usable DRAM, which put the ramdisk at
0x8e562000 and the FDT at 0x8e55b000 -- inside the 105 MiB ION carveout at
0x89500000 that the kernel DTS reserves for the video pipeline (meta-nanokvm
patch 0011, mirroring CVIMMAP_ION_ADDR). The kernel reserves initrd and FDT
first, so the no-map region then overlapped an existing reservation and was
rejected outright:

  OF: reserved mem: Reserved memory: failed to reserve memory for node
      'ion@89500000': base 0x0000000089500000, size 105 MiB

leaving the carveout heap registered with base 0x0 size 0x0 -- every
sys_ion_alloc() in the capture stack would fail. 0x9500000 bounds the bootm
region to [0x80000000, 0x89500000), i.e. exactly up to the carveout base, so
it must stay in sync with CVIMMAP_ION_ADDR and the DTS reservation.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NanoKVM boot-flow specific; upstream
should grow a full distro-boot memory map instead]
---
--- a/include/configs/licheerv_nano.h
+++ b/include/configs/licheerv_nano.h
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@
 								"baudrate=115200\0" \
+								"bootm_size=0x9500000\0" \
 								"fdt_addr_r=0x82000000\0" \
 								"kernel_addr_r=0x81000000\0" \
+								"ramdisk_addr_r=0x84000000\0" \
 								"scriptaddr=0x80c00000\0" \
 								BOOTENV
 
